{"id": "H09", "category": "docs", "question": "Who presses harder, Aston Villa or Wolves?", "answer": "Based on internal club documents describing team styles and tendencies (note that these describe style and do not explain match results):\n\n* **Aston Villa:** Their pre-match briefing (`02_briefing_aston_villa.md`) notes that they approach fixtures in a compact mid-to-high block, aggressively stepping up with a PPDA of **9.8**, highlighting high pressing intensity in the middle third.\n* **Wolverhampton Wanderers:** Their pre-match briefing (`12_briefing_wolves.md`) states that they maintain a highly organized low block and record a PPDA of **16.2**, indicating a complete refusal to press high up the pitch.\n\nTherefore, **Aston Villa** presses significantly harder than Wolverhampton Wanderers.", "tools": ["search_documents"], "tool_calls": [{"tool": "search_documents", "args": {"query": "Aston Villa pressing Wolves pressing"}, "duration_ms": 200.9, "error": null, "response_preview": "{\"query\": \"Aston Villa pressing Wolves pressing\", \"results\": [{\"source_file\": \"02_briefing_aston_villa.md\", \"title\": \"Pre-Match Briefing: Aston Villa (Matchday 9)\", \"date\": \"2023-10-20\", \"content\": \"### Pre-Match Briefing: Aston Villa (Matchday 9)\\n**Date:** 20 October 2023  \\n**Author:** Marcus Que"}], "latency_s": 2.98, "input_tokens": 2915, "output_tokens": 174, "thought_tokens": 0, "model_calls": 2, "attempts": 1, "error": null, "status": "pass", "tool_ok": true, "reasons": []}
